    "# Zoo Classifier: Cats vs. Dogs vs. Pandas\n",
    "\n",
    "**Approach (Option 2):** transfer learning with a pretrained VGG19 backbone, compared against a small from-scratch CNN baseline.\n",
    "Output layer: 3-way softmax. Loss: `categorical_crossentropy`.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Step 1: Data Exploration\n",
    "Before any modeling we need to understand the dataset: how many images there are, whether the classes are balanced,\n",
    "whether any files are broken, how image dimensions vary, and what the images look like. These findings decide the\n",
    "input size and preprocessing used in later steps."
   ],
   "id": "3b3fd9d4dfa14f03"
  },
  {
   "metadata": {},
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "source": [
    "### 1.1 Imports and configuration\n",
    "Only light-weight libraries are needed for exploration. A fixed seed keeps the random image samples reproducible."
